## What Has NOT Been Tried Yet (deferred code-phase — PRIORITY ORDER)

1. **finding #2 — EPREV cosmetic → PASS-with-cleanup, not REVISE.** The doom-loop TRIGGER. Auto-strip/ignore cosmetic JSON fields (no logos / continuity_anchors empty / policy_notes) instead of REVISE. Without it the loop recurs on ANY shot.
2. **Shot-level regen cap** (not per-plan): count TOTAL image-gens + plan-regens PER SHOT (across all plan versions) → N(3-5) → HALT+escalate. Closes the gap that let SH23 hit 45 images.
3. **Cap EXEC-EREF-DESIGNER (plan regen) per shot** — 58 plan versions impossible by construction.
4. **Cap Polina auto-recovery per shot** — her regenerateRefPlan fired 39× on SH23; apply critic-revision-cap to designer↔EPREV loop.
5. **Loud Anthropic→gemini fallback** (Director's idea): creators stay Sonnet by default; on Anthropic error (credit/rate/5xx) auto-retry gemini-free + stamp provider_fallback + stat. Never hard-stop on billing.
6. **Pipeline UI provider badge** — replace redundant role label ("DESIGNER"/"CRITIC") with the model used (gemini-free/sonnet/gpt-image). Makes fallbacks visible.
7. **REVISION→APPROVED for human Director** — allow REVISION/NEEDS_HUMAN_TWEAK → APPROVED when approver is human (Director-edited assets need no agent re-review/2nd approval). Add "Save & Approve" button.
8. **buildShotListFromAnchorChain failure** — EXEC-EDIT animatic rebuild failed ×3 during SH22/SH23 churn; investigate.

